## At a glance

| Stage | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| Input | MQTT telemetry |
| Processing | Streaming pipelines |
| Calibration | Conformal scores |
| Output | Reviewable evidence |

A stream leaves the band its baseline was calibrated to. Evidence accumulates with every observation until the change is flagged: a change point τ is reported once the evidence reaches 1/α.

## How it works

See the change in context, from connected sensor streams to evidence you can explore.

1. **Observe — read the relationships.** Bring your sensor streams together. See how measurements behave in relation to one another, beyond individual readings.
2. **Calibrate — establish the reference.** Learn from baseline data and calibrate anomaly scores with conformal methods. Give new observations a meaningful reference.
3. **Detect — follow the evidence.** Accumulate evidence as observations arrive. Explore detected changes alongside the telemetry that explains them.

